00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:34,950
这里就有不同的层次，
So, here we have different levels.

351
00:19:34,950 --> 00:19:36,280
穷人有着很低的收入，
Poor people with low income,

352
00:19:36,290 --> 00:19:37,950
随着社会层次越高收入就越高。
and then progressively higher income.

353
00:19:37,950 --> 00:19:42,260
下面这三层代表了50%人口的收入——
These three shelves represent 50% of the population --

354
00:19:42,260 --> 00:19:44,430
也就是人口数目的一半——
a half of the population --

355
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:47,150
这一半人口的总收入就是
and all this total income of the half of the population,

356
00:19:47,150 --> 00:19:49,600
你可以数下金条数量，100根金条里只有10根。
you count these bars, it's only 10 bars out of 100.

357
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,520
换句话说，下层一半人口的收入
In other words, the lower 50% of population

358
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:55,800
只占了整个系统总收入的10%。
receives only 10% of total income of the system.

359
00:19:55,810 --> 00:19:57,520
这就是收入的差异。
That's income inequality.

360
00:19:57,520 --> 00:20:02,310
这些贫富差距，
This imbalance between the haves and have nots,

361
00:20:02,310 --> 00:20:06,450
虽然非常剧烈，但并不只美国是这样。
though dramatic, is not unique to the U.S.

362
00:20:06,450 --> 00:20:08,780
任何社会都存在这种不均衡--
Pretty much any society has inequality --

363
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:11,170
少数富人，多数穷人--
a few rich people, many poor people --

364
00:20:11,170 --> 00:20:13,090
而且这一特征持续出现在
and it's a persistent feature

365
00:20:13,090 --> 00:20:14,820
几乎所有的社会中。
of pretty much all societies.

366
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:15,960
于是我认为，
And so I said,

367
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:18,460
可能存在某种深层次的原因，
maybe there's some kind of deep reason for this,

368
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:21,850
也许我们能够利用物理知识来解释这种现象。
and maybe we can understand them by knowledge of its physics.

369
00:20:21,850 --> 00:20:25,020
Victor利用物理学概念，
Victor took concepts from physics,

370
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:27,940
比如分子的运动，
such as the behavior of molecules,

371
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:30,940
应用于金融数据中。
and applied them to financial data.

372
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,060
他发现所有的国家中，
He discovered that in virtually all countries,

373
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:36,440
只存在富人的经济
there is the economy of the rich

374
00:20:36,450 --> 00:20:40,060
和与之完全不同的普通人经济。
and a very different economy for everyone else.

375
00:20:40,070 --> 00:20:46,450
在美国，3%的富人年收入超过15万美元，
In America, the 3% with incomes greater than $150,000 a year

376
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:48,570
他们生活其中的规律
might as well live in a different reality

377
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,360
和其余97%的人是不同的。
than the less well-off 97%.

378
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:56,160
Victor称之为热力学和超热力学经济。
Victor calls them the thermal and the superthermal economies.

379
00:20:56,170 --> 00:21:00,370
这两种经济和物理学规律有着诡异的相似性。
Each behaves in ways physicists find eerily familiar.

380
00:21:00,370 --> 00:21:02,890
这有一锅开水，
Consider this pot of boiling water.

381
00:21:02,890 --> 00:21:05,970
锅里的水分子剧烈运动，
The water molecules in the pot jiggle around

382
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:09,230
互相碰撞，无明显顺序，
and bump into each other with no apparent order,

383
00:21:09,230 --> 00:21:12,380
但这些随机运动符合一种规律
but these random movements actually fit a pattern

384
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:14,430
即玻尔兹曼分布。
called a Boltzmann distribution.

385
00:21:14,430 --> 00:21:17,720
它描述了物质粒子
It describes how energy is spread between particles

386
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:20,270
处于热力学稳定状态时能量的分布。
when they achieve thermal equilibrium.

387
00:21:20,270 --> 00:21:22,610
物理学分布中我们能够看到
So, we see this distribution in physics

388
00:21:22,610 --> 00:21:25,190
原子互相碰撞和能量的重新分布，
when atoms collide and redistribute energy,

389
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:27,530
而我们在金钱的分布中
but we also see the same distribution

390
00:21:27,530 --> 00:21:28,950
也发现了同样的模式。
in distribution of money.

391
00:21:28,950 --> 00:21:30,870
非常奇怪
Strangely enough,

392
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:35,200
这就是金钱在97%人口中的分布。
this is how money is scattered across 97% of the population.

393
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:39,170
就算每人的初始现金都一样，
Even if everyone starts out with equal amounts of cash,

394
00:21:39,180 --> 00:21:43,540
随着时间延续，就会呈现出玻尔兹曼分布。
over time, the money spreads out in a Boltzmann distribution.

395
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:46,510
会有大部分人处于中间，
There will be lots of people in the middle,

396
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:51,300
小部分人非常贫穷或相对富有，
and fewer who are very poor or relatively wealthy,

397
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:55,810
但对于顶层的3%来说，就是另外一回事了。
but for the 3% at the top, it's a very different story.

398
00:21:55,810 --> 00:21:58,030
在热力学经济中
The thermal economy gives way

399
00:21:58,030 --> 00:22:01,610
Victor称之为超热力学经济。
to what Victor calls the superthermal economy.

400
00:22:01,610 --> 00:22:06,030
超热力学经济就像是高能分子
The superthermal economy is like the high-energy molecules

401
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:10,150
可以通过蒸汽的形式从开水中释放出来。
that break free of boiling water and escape as steam.

402
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:14,130
水分子有特定的温度，
The molecules of water, they have certain temperature.

403
00:22:14,130 --> 00:22:16,610
蒸汽就像是上层社会，
So the vapor here would be the analog of the upper class,

404
00:22:16,610 --> 00:22:17,960
这里的分子
because these are the molecules

405
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,550
有着最高的能量。
with the highest possible energy.

406
00:22:19,550 --> 00:22:22,130
这些高能分子
These high-energy molecules

407
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:24,550
就不再遵循玻尔兹曼分布。
no longer follow a Boltzmann distribution.

408
00:22:24,550 --> 00:22:28,920
相反，他们遵循幂次分布，
Instead, they are governed by a power law,

409
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:32,090
这种分布没有上限。
a distribution that has no upper limit.

410
00:22:35,150 --> 00:22:39,980
那么为什么两种经济体有两套不同的法则？
So, why are there two economies with two sets of rules?

411
00:22:39,990 --> 00:22:43,320
下层阶级的97%的人口
The 97% of the population in the lower classes

412
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:46,240
以自己获得的薪水生活。
live off the money from their paycheck.

413
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:49,830
同时，上层阶级则把金钱投资到
Meanwhile, the upper class invests its money

414
00:22:49,830 --> 00:22:52,280
金融市场和财产当中。
in financial markets and property.

415
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:55,200
不像人们靠工资生活，
Unlike people living on a fixed wage,

416
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:57,950
富人的金钱是
the rich have their money in a part of the economy

417
00:22:57,950 --> 00:22:59,790
无上限的经济的一部分。
that has no limits.

418
00:22:59,790 --> 00:23:04,430
就像蒸汽，从锅中散出。
Like steam, it has escaped the boundaries of the pot.

419
00:23:04,430 --> 00:23:07,460
这种模式贯穿人类历史，
The pattern stretches across history

420
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:09,680
从古埃及，再到今天。
from ancient Egypt to today.

421
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:13,050
无论一个国家开始时是多么平等，
No matter how equal a nation starts,

422
00:23:13,050 --> 00:23:16,300
最后都会进入这种模式。
this pattern seems to take over.

423
00:23:16,310 --> 00:23:18,520
比如以色列，
Take Israel.

424
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:20,940
在1948年建国时，
When formed in 1948,

425
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:25,360
以色列是一个有着社会主义色彩的高度平等的国家。
Israel was a highly egalitarian country with a socialist bent.

426
00:23:25,370 --> 00:23:30,650
通过计划，人们的收入差不多一样，
By design, people had more or less the same income.

427
00:23:30,650 --> 00:23:34,190
但以色列的收入分布逐渐扩大了，
But Israel's income distribution slowly broadened,

428
00:23:34,190 --> 00:23:38,710
到了1990年，就形成了
and by 1990, it, too, had reached the shape

429
00:23:38,710 --> 00:23:41,910
热力学经济的收入分布。
of a thermal economy.

430
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,050
四十年里，
So, in 40 years or so,

431
00:23:43,050 --> 00:23:45,000
他们从高度平均的分布
it evolved from highly equal distribution

432
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,720
扩展到这种不均衡分布，
to this broad unequal distribution,

433
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:50,700
我认为这之后还会发展出上层阶级，
and after that, I believe, it developed upper class,

434
00:23:50,710 --> 00:23:54,040
进入超热力学模式，造成更剧烈的不均衡。
the superthermal tail, even higher inequality.

435
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:58,350
平均，完美的平均，是非常不稳定的，
Equality, perfect equality, is totally unstable. Okay?

436
00:23:58,350 --> 00:24:00,680
一旦进入这种状态，
Once you engage into any transaction,

437
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,150
就毫无平均可言了。
equality goes away.

438
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:07,990
超级富人操纵着自己的物理学法则，
The super rich operate by their own separate physical laws,

439
00:24:07,990 --> 00:24:13,660
但他们仍要同穷人一起生活在地球上。
but they have to live on the same planet as the poor.

440
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:18,870
生物学中也许隐藏着这种共同生存的关键。
Biology could hold the key to our mutual survival.

441
00:24:22,870 --> 00:24:26,130
查尔斯·达尔文认为地球生命
Charles Darwin saw life on earth

442
00:24:26,250 --> 00:24:29,280
都想尽一切办法生存，
as a bitter struggle for survival.

443
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:31,470
富人就像全权负责了财富，
That seems like carte blanche

444
00:24:31,470 --> 00:24:34,420
可以拿走任何想要的东西。
for the rich to take what they want.

445
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:35,960
贪婪才是生存之道，
Greed is king,

446
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:40,460
但我们对进化的理解也在进步。
but our understanding of evolution is evolving.

447
00:24:40,460 --> 00:24:45,730
合作和团结也许和自私一样
Cooperation and community may be just as essential

448
00:24:45,730 --> 00:24:49,740
对于生存非常重要。
to our survival as selfishness.

449
00:24:53,110 --> 00:24:58,080
Tracy Mincer研究的是地球上最古老的集体：
Tracy Mincer studies the oldest communities on earth:

450
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:00,200
微生物集落。
Colonies of microbes.

451
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:04,200
Tracy就职于伍兹霍尔海洋研究所，
Working out of the Woods Hole Oceanographic Institute

452
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,650
位于马萨诸塞州，
in Massachusetts,

453
00:25:05,650 --> 00:25:08,840
他和他的微生物学家团队
Tracy and his team of microbiologists

454
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:14,010
环游世界搜集奇异的微生物。
travel the world gathering exotic microorganisms.

455
00:25:14,010 --> 00:25:15,800
我感觉自己就像在
I feel like I'm really looking

456
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:19,000
观察地球上剩余待开发的荒野，
at some of the last wilderness left on earth to explore

457
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:23,500
而它们就在我们的试管中。
because what we're seeing is wilderness in a tube.

458
00:25:23,510 --> 00:25:27,140
我们从野生资源中搜集微生物，
We're harvesting microbes from their wild sources

459
00:25:27,140 --> 00:25:29,860
来观察它们是如何工作的。
and looking at how they're working.

460
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:34,870
单细胞生物无处不在：
Single-celled organisms are everywhere:

461
00:25:34,870 --> 00:25:39,490
土壤、树木，包括我们的身体里。
In the soil, in the trees, in our bodies.

462
00:25:39,490 --> 00:25:42,990
它们处于进化的基层，
They were at the ground floor of evolution,

463
00:25:42,990 --> 00:25:44,740
可它们太小了，
but they are so tiny,

464
00:25:44,740 --> 00:25:48,250
在我们眼中几百万个微生物只有针尖大小。
millions can fit into the eye of a needle.

465
00:25:48,250 --> 00:25:49,660
直到最近，
Until recently,

466
00:25:49,670 --> 00:25:53,370
我们能够看到这些生物是如何集体生存的。
we could only see how these creatures functioned as a group.

467
00:25:53,370 --> 00:25:56,840
我们看不到单个微生物体内
We couldn't see the molecular processes happening

468
00:25:56,840 --> 00:25:58,890
发生的分子进程，
inside individual microbes.

469
00:25:58,890 --> 00:26:01,420
但现在一切都有所改变。
But that has all changed.

470
00:26:03,930 --> 00:26:06,900
现阶段是非常激动人心的，
It's a very exciting time right now,

471
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:11,150
因为我们能够研究
because we can look at really big questions

472
00:26:11,150 --> 00:26:15,660
40或50年前我们提出的大问题，
that were asked 40 or 50 years ago in science

473
00:26:15,660 --> 00:26:17,390
这些问题当时无法回答
but were unanswerable

474
00:26:17,390 --> 00:26:21,240
因为受限于技术手段。
because of the limitations in the technical tools.

475
00:26:21,250 --> 00:26:23,830
现在，基因组学发生了革命性变化，
Now, with the revolution in genomics

476
00:26:23,830 --> 00:26:27,080
测序、分子生物学和克隆，
and sequencing and molecular biology and cloning,

477
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:30,070
我们就能够看到单个细胞的生长，
we can look at a single cell that's growing

478
00:26:30,070 --> 00:26:33,570
还有它体内产生的信号，
and see the signals that are being produced from it

479
00:26:33,580 --> 00:26:37,340
这样在单细胞水平上了解都发生了什么。
and understand what's happening at that single-cell level.

480
00:26:38,750 --> 00:26:41,850
人们认为微生物会遵守
One would expect microbes to be ruled

481
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:44,420
自然界中最基本的法则，
by the most basic laws of nature,

482
00:26:44,420 --> 00:26:46,190
适者生存，
survival of the fittest,

483
00:26:46,190 --> 00:26:49,190
任何生物都要为自己拼搏，
where every organism fights for itself,

484
00:26:49,190 --> 00:26:53,140
但Tracy发现即使这些简单生物
but Tracy has found that even these simple creatures

485
00:26:53,150 --> 00:26:55,930
也具有合作精神。
are capable of cooperation.

486
00:26:55,930 --> 00:26:59,530
Tracy观察了多株海洋细菌，
Tracy watches how different strains of marine bacteria

487
00:26:59,530 --> 00:27:03,570
看它们如何防御捕食者的攻击。
defend themselves against predators.

488
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:06,660
他取了一株叫做Vibrio Ordalii的细菌培养在培养皿中，
He places a strain of vibrio ordalii,

489
00:27:06,660 --> 00:27:11,040
这种细菌会引起鱼类疾病。
a bacterium that causes disease in fish, in a petri dish.

490
00:27:11,050 --> 00:27:13,110
然后加入丰年虾，
Then he adds brine shrimp,

491
00:27:13,110 --> 00:27:16,550
它是这种细菌的捕食者。
predators that like to munch on bacterium.

492
00:27:16,550 --> 00:27:17,920
作为自我防御机制，
In self defense,

493
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:22,010
有一些Vibrio细菌开始产生毒素，
some of the vibrio bacteria begin to produce a toxin

494
00:27:22,010 --> 00:27:25,140
这样就能杀死捕食者丰年虾。
that kills the predatory brine shrimp.

495
00:27:25,140 --> 00:27:29,060
这种毒素不会杀死Vibrio细菌的亲缘菌，
This toxin does not kill vibrio's closest relatives,

496
00:27:29,060 --> 00:27:32,520
这些细菌就是生物学家称作的种群。
the members of what biologists call its guild.

497
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:35,650
令我们震惊的是这些细菌
What's striking is that they never killed

498
00:27:35,650 --> 00:27:37,440
从来没被自己的种群杀死过。
within their own guild.

499
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,310
这种杀伤作用只体现在对外。
They killed only outside.

500
00:27:39,310 --> 00:27:41,640
更令人惊讶的是，
Even more surprisingly,

501
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:45,980
当它们杀死丰年虾时，
the bacteria that make the antibiotics sacrifice themselves

502
00:27:45,980 --> 00:27:48,370
细菌会牺牲自己产生抗生素，
when they kill the brine shrimp.

503
00:27:48,370 --> 00:27:52,670
通过牺牲一小部分，它们保护了整个种群。
By taking one for the team, they protect the entire group.

504
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:56,670
在微生物层面就已存在利他主义：
Down at the level of microbes, we see altruism:

505
00:27:56,680 --> 00:28:00,540
为集体的利益牺牲自己。
Self-sacrifice for the good of the community.

506
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:04,460
利他主义适用于微生物，
Altruism holds for microbes,

507
00:28:04,470 --> 00:28:08,500
由于这种种群型的构造，
because of these guild-type structures

508
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:12,010
即个体的牺牲使微生物种群得以生存，
where it really is for the betterment of the microbes

509
00:28:12,010 --> 00:28:15,510
这的确非常有利。
to be able to sacrifice.

510
00:28:15,510 --> 00:28:18,060
当然生物并不总是在
So, things aren't always fighting to the death

511
00:28:18,060 --> 00:28:19,060
对抗死亡，
at all times.

512
00:28:19,060 --> 00:28:22,400
生存需要团结。
It takes a group effort.

513
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:24,780
对于生物的合作来说，
For organisms to cooperate,

514
00:28:24,790 --> 00:28:26,520
首先它们要学会交流，
they need to communicate,

515
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:31,520
就像Tracy的团队合作搜集样本。
the way that Tracy's team works to gather samples.

516
00:28:31,530 --> 00:28:35,250
但无脑或无声带的生物
But how do creatures with no brains or vocal chords

517
00:28:35,250 --> 00:28:38,870
如何才能传递信息来共同行动呢？
convey a message that causes them to act together?

518
00:28:42,090 --> 00:28:45,060
答案就埋藏在自然界中。
The answer is embedded in nature.

519
00:28:45,060 --> 00:28:49,540
存在一种我们无法看到的化学形式的交流，
There is a chemical form of communication we cannot see

520
00:28:49,540 --> 00:28:52,880
却又是生命的基本部分。
