are shared among all the herdsmen,

693
00:37:17,480 --> 00:37:19,930
这就是公地悲剧：
and this is the tragedy of the commons:

694
00:37:19,930 --> 00:37:22,780
个体与群体间的紧张关系。
The tension between the individual and the group.

695
00:37:22,780 --> 00:37:25,570
真正的问题是如果一个牧人
And the real problem is that just one herdsman

696
00:37:25,570 --> 00:37:27,650
决定增加很多头牛，
who decides to add too many cattle

697
00:37:27,650 --> 00:37:31,150
这就可能对所有人造成影响。
can ruin it for everybody else.

698
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:35,240
Jennifer认为，公地悲剧
The tragedy of the commons, Jennifer says,

699
00:37:35,240 --> 00:37:37,330
现在是全球性的悲剧，
is now a global tragedy,

700
00:37:37,330 --> 00:37:40,630
这场悲剧被
a tragedy that is being accelerated

701
00:37:40,630 --> 00:37:44,050
超级富豪的私欲所加速。
by the selfishness of the super rich.

702
00:37:44,050 --> 00:37:46,800
我们有着全球性的海洋，
There's the global oceans.

703
00:37:46,810 --> 00:37:48,390
共同的大气，
There's the atmosphere.

704
00:37:48,390 --> 00:37:50,460
还有全球性的森林，
There are the global forests.

705
00:37:50,460 --> 00:37:52,120
以及迁徙的鸟类，
There are migratory birds.

706
00:37:52,130 --> 00:37:53,730
有很多事物
There are so many things

707
00:37:53,730 --> 00:37:57,260
其实都像是公地，
that behave exactly like this common pasture.

708
00:37:57,270 --> 00:37:58,650
我们现在生活在一个
So we now live in a world

709
00:37:58,650 --> 00:38:00,850
极少数人
in which a very small minority of people

710
00:38:00,850 --> 00:38:03,240
可以毁掉其他所有人的世界中，
is capable of ruining it for everyone else.

711
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:06,690
通常社会利用法律准则
Typically, society keeps citizens in line

712
00:38:06,690 --> 00:38:08,240
来约束人民，
by the rule of law.

713
00:38:08,240 --> 00:38:09,980
但纵观全球，
But around the world,

714
00:38:09,980 --> 00:38:14,310
极富之人通常能够规避法律，
the extremely wealthy are often able to circumvent the law

715
00:38:14,320 --> 00:38:17,200
或是改变法律条文以方便自己。
or have laws changed to suit them.

716
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:19,650
那我们应该如何才能制止这些人
So how do we stop these people

717
00:38:19,650 --> 00:38:22,710
消耗掉我们共同享有的资源？
from depleting our shared resources?

718
00:38:22,710 --> 00:38:26,160
革命就是争取权利的一种手段，
Revolutions have been fought over such things,

719
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:32,850
而Jennifer认为我们唯一明智的手段就是羞耻。
but Jennifer argues the only sensible recourse is shame.

720
00:38:32,850 --> 00:38:34,180
当我们谈到羞耻，
So, when we talk about shame,

721
00:38:34,190 --> 00:38:36,300
其实说的是一种工具，
what we're actually talking about is a tool,

722
00:38:36,300 --> 00:38:37,300
一种惩罚。
a type of punishment.

723
00:38:37,310 --> 00:38:38,860
将某人某事曝光，
The threat of exposure,

724
00:38:38,860 --> 00:38:41,470
这种观念就是向周围的人
this idea that we could show the crowd

725
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:43,360
展示出你并没有
that you haven't been behaving

726
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:46,010
像其他人一样遵守行为准则，
like the rest of the group would like,

727
00:38:46,010 --> 00:38:48,510
这种羞耻也是我正在检验的。
this is the type of shame I examine.

728
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:52,400
今天，Jennifer正在做一项实验
Today, Jennifer is running an experiment

729
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:55,540
来证明羞耻的力量。
demonstrating the power of shame.

730
00:38:55,540 --> 00:38:58,690
这项实验展示出了人们在
It reveals the difference in people's behavior

731
00:38:58,690 --> 00:39:00,710
自己能够隐瞒起来
when their identities are hidden

732
00:39:00,710 --> 00:39:04,130
和自己的行为被曝光之间的不同表现。
versus when their actions are exposed to the group.

733
00:39:04,130 --> 00:39:08,920
每位受试者都要选择向公共资源
Each player is given the choice to contribute or not contribute

734
00:39:08,920 --> 00:39:10,390
捐钱或不捐钱。
to a common pool.

735
00:39:10,390 --> 00:39:14,010
无论怎样进入公共资源的钱
Whatever money goes into the common pool

736
00:39:14,010 --> 00:39:17,090
会翻倍然后重新分给受试者。
is doubled and then redistributed.

737
00:39:17,100 --> 00:39:19,650
如果每人每轮都捐出一美元，
If everybody puts in a dollar,

738
00:39:19,650 --> 00:39:23,520
每10轮后，他们就能得到20美元，
in each of 10 rounds, they all get $20 back.

739
00:39:23,520 --> 00:39:26,100
前提是，他们必须要公平游戏。
That is, if they all play fair.

740
00:39:26,100 --> 00:39:29,390
可公平游戏基本上是不可能的，
That almost is never the way the game is played.

741
00:39:29,390 --> 00:39:31,520
人们的行为总会导致
People often leave with far less

742
00:39:31,530 --> 00:39:34,030
无法达到最佳社会结果，
than the socially optimal outcome,

743
00:39:34,030 --> 00:39:36,730
这是因为总有一些社会个体
and that's because certain individuals

744
00:39:36,730 --> 00:39:39,500
从中脱离或不予合作。
start pulling out and stop cooperating.

745
00:39:39,500 --> 00:39:42,620
大多数人都捐了钱，
Most contribute to the common pool,

746
00:39:42,620 --> 00:39:44,570
除了这些人，
except these players.

747
00:39:44,570 --> 00:39:46,040
他们留下了自己拥有的10美元，
They keep their $10,

748
00:39:46,040 --> 00:39:49,960
但仍从翻倍的共同资源中拿走与其他人等量的钱，
but still take an equal share from the doubled communal pot.

749
00:39:49,960 --> 00:39:54,300
这样最后得到的会比其他人多，
So they end up making more than their classmates,

750
00:39:54,300 --> 00:39:56,430
他们能够侥幸成功，
and they get away with it

751
00:39:56,430 --> 00:39:59,690
因为没人知道谁在作弊。
because no one knows who is cheating.

752
00:39:59,690 --> 00:40:02,690
现在Jennifer又做了个实验，
But now Jennifer runs the experiment again,

753
00:40:02,690 --> 00:40:04,810
并加入了羞耻的元素。
adding in the element of shame.

754
00:40:04,810 --> 00:40:06,690
在第十轮的最后时刻，
At the end of the 10th round,

755
00:40:06,690 --> 00:40:09,280
捐款最少的
the real names of the two participants

756
00:40:09,280 --> 00:40:10,950
两个人的名字
who donated least overall

757
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:13,320
会向其他玩家公布。
are revealed to the other players.

758
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:16,040
会被曝光的威胁
The threat of being exposed

759
00:40:16,040 --> 00:40:18,270
改变了人们的游戏方式，
changes the way people play.

760
00:40:18,270 --> 00:40:24,080
现在几乎所有人都捐出了公平份额。
Now almost everyone puts in their fair share.

761
00:40:24,080 --> 00:40:25,610
羞耻带来的威胁
So the threat of shame

762
00:40:25,610 --> 00:40:28,160
促进了合作，
actually led to 50% more cooperation

763
00:40:28,170 --> 00:40:31,500
合作比匿名对照组增加了50%。
than the anonymous -- completely anonymous control.

764
00:40:33,500 --> 00:40:37,620
那么这种作用在真实世界中是如何进行的？
So, what are the real-world effects of this?

765
00:40:37,630 --> 00:40:39,310
2008年，
So, in 2008,

766
00:40:39,310 --> 00:40:43,150
美国政府拨给银行2450亿美元的
the United States government gave banks $245 billion

767
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:44,600
援助资金。
in bailout money.

768
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:47,730
许多银行决定拿走
Many of the banks decided to give bonuses

769
00:40:47,740 --> 00:40:49,850
总计200亿美元的红利。
that added up to $20 billion.

770
00:40:49,850 --> 00:40:51,070
那个时候
During that time,

771
00:40:51,070 --> 00:40:54,140
奥巴马总统称这些红利是“羞耻的”，
President Obama called those bonuses "shameful,"

772
00:40:54,140 --> 00:40:57,330
这可能是因为还没有正式的机制
and that's in part because there was no formal mechanism

773
00:40:57,330 --> 00:41:01,450
来处罚这么做的银行。
in which to punish the banks for having done that.

774
00:41:01,450 --> 00:41:04,150
于是他号召人们加入反对并称：
So he sort of called on the crowd to come in and say,

775
00:41:04,150 --> 00:41:06,840
“这种行为是不合适的。”
"this is not appropriate behavior."

776
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:09,010
许多银行家并不这么认为。
Many bankers didn't see it that way.

777
00:41:09,010 --> 00:41:12,380
他们认为这是完全正常的行为。
They saw it as perfectly normal behavior.

778
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:16,850
羞耻的行为通常出现在旁观者眼中，
Shameful behavior is in the eye of the beholder.

779
00:41:16,850 --> 00:41:19,020
大多数超级富豪则认为
Most of the super rich would argue

780
00:41:19,020 --> 00:41:21,020
自己并没有打破社会规则，
they are not breaking any social rules.

781
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:23,800
实际上，他们的投资创造了就业机会，
In fact, their investments create jobs

782
00:41:23,810 --> 00:41:27,020
并推动整个经济繁荣发展。
and make the entire economy thrive and grow.

783
00:41:27,030 --> 00:41:31,110
但所有阶层总会有少数人
But there will always be a few people at any income level

784
00:41:31,110 --> 00:41:34,230
想要骗取利益。
who are willing to cheat to make a profit.

785
00:41:34,230 --> 00:41:39,290
当这些人被公布于公众面前
When those people are called out by name in front of a crowd,

786
00:41:39,290 --> 00:41:41,350
羞耻是很有效的。
shame can be effective.

787
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:44,460
加州已经开始将本州内的前500名
California has started listing the names

788
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:48,040
拖欠税款人员公布在网上，
of the state's top 500 tax delinquents online,

789
00:41:48,050 --> 00:41:54,000
通过羞愧手段促使他们付出自己应付的部分。
using shame to coerce them to pay their fair share.

790
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,750
但只是羞耻的力量
But is the power of shame enough

791
00:41:56,750 --> 00:42:00,010
就足够弥补贫富间差距吗？
to close the gap between rich and poor?

792
00:42:00,010 --> 00:42:02,710
解决办法当然不会这么简单，
There are no simple solutions, of course.

793
00:42:02,710 --> 00:42:05,380
这些问题非常庞大和困难，
These problems are -- are gigantic and difficult.

794
00:42:05,380 --> 00:42:09,230
羞耻是种相对廉价、
Shame is relatively cheap in terms of punishment,

795
00:42:09,230 --> 00:42:11,380
相对低效的惩罚手段。
and relatively ineffective.

796
00:42:11,390 --> 00:42:13,220
但有时这是我们唯一能做的。
But sometimes it's all we have.

797
00:42:17,220 --> 00:42:23,600
我就是个贫穷并不会遗传的例子，
I am living proof that poverty is not genetic.

798
00:42:23,600 --> 00:42:26,600
我的生活既贫穷过，
I've lived on both sides of the divide

799
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:28,370
也富有过，
between rich and poor.

800
00:42:28,370 --> 00:42:32,740
财富分配的力量是复杂的，
The forces that distribute wealth among us are complicated.

801
00:42:32,740 --> 00:42:37,010
混合了生物学、心理学以及数学，
They're a mixture of biology, psychology, and mathematics

802
00:42:37,010 --> 00:42:39,210
在我们的生命中发挥着重要作用，
playing out over lifetimes

803
00:42:39,210 --> 00:42:42,420
更是贯穿了整个人类历史。
and across the sweep of human history.

804
00:42:42,420 --> 00:42:45,420
如果我们能够了解这些力量，
If we can understand those forces,

805
00:42:45,420 --> 00:42:49,730
我希望有朝一日能够减小贫穷的影响，
I hope we can someday lessen the devastation of poverty

806
00:42:49,730 --> 00:42:52,970
让每个人都能充分发挥自己的潜能。
and allow each of us to reach our full potential.

